+### Physical desktop Q
+
+In host desktop builds, a fresh unmodified physical **Q** requests the normal application exit
+from ordinary pages and the player, with either Classic or Modern presentation. The existing
+shutdown sequence checkpoints playback, drains pending work, and follows its verified-write
+policy; the keyboard handler does not write settings or terminate the process directly.
+
+Q key edges in text-capable Search, OTT editors, and owned keyboard fields stay with text input.
+The separate SDL text event inserts the character once, including **Shift+Q**. Shift/Ctrl/Alt/GUI-Q
+do not gain an application-exit shortcut; Caps/Num lock alone do not disable plain Q. Modal
+confirmation and parental surfaces, pending navigation, active controls, setup, and queued input
+retain ownership. Strict kiosk and pending kiosk transitions keep their existing input fences.
+The first key in Standby still wakes only.
+
+The physical Q release belongs to the same gesture even if focus or modifiers changed. Repeats
+never become fresh Quit requests. Injected remote Q and native television Back/Q keep their
+existing Back mapping; Escape remains Back. Physical desktop Quit is not encoded in the current
+controlled recording format and therefore refuses recording rather than creating a misleading tape.
